# TestWeb — a concrete, DETERMINISTIC web_tool adapter. Declares its family
# (web_tool) — the inverted arrow ; the family never names it. Named for its
# IDENTITY (a fixture-backed test provider), NOT its transport. Mirrors
# adapters/llm/test-llm.adapter.
#
# The `handler` is the OUT-OF-PROCESS program the inline primary-adapter wait
# (Runtime::drain_outbound_to_quiescence) execs when the bound event fires : it
# reads the event payload on stdin (carries `url` for fetch / `query` for search
# + `tool`), looks up a DETERMINISTIC fixture keyed by the request (NO real
# network), and writes `output=<body>` to stdout, exit 0. The drainer (NOT the
# handler) dispatches the success verdict + marks the delivery delivered — the
# payment/verdict-capturing protocol, not tts's self-ack.
#
# Fixture lookup mirrors the llm-handler's TSV shape : $WEB_TOOL_FIXTURES points
# at a `key<TAB>output` file where key is `<tool>:<url-or-query>`. A miss yields
# the deterministic lenient placeholder `[test-web:unknown <tool>=<arg>]`.
Hecks.adapter "TestWeb" do
  family  "web_tool"
  handler "adapters/web_tool/web-tool-handler"
end
